catalog.json is generated by internal/catalogimport. It contains facts from:

- mason registry (https://github.com/mason-org/mason-registry),
  Apache License 2.0. Release and SHA-256: internal/catalogimport/pins.json.
- Helix languages.toml (https://github.com/helix-editor/helix),
  Mozilla Public License 2.0. Commit and SHA-256: internal/catalogimport/pins.json.
  Source code for MPL-covered data is available at that commit.
- GitHub Linguist language data through go-enry
  (https://github.com/go-enry/go-enry): Linguist data under the MIT license,
  go-enry under the Apache License 2.0.

authored.json is original Crude data, except the off_side, folding_markers and editing
facts. Those copy folding.offSide, folding.markers, brackets, onEnterRules and
indentationRules of VS Code's
built-in language configurations
(https://github.com/microsoft/vscode, extensions/*/language-configuration.json),
MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. Each entry names its file and
commit.
